<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan tightens belts of state-run banks.</title>
<headline>Pakistan tightens belts of state-run banks.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's caretaker cabinet announced stringent measures on Wednesday to cut &quot;wasteful expenditure&quot; of state-run banks and financial institutions.</p>
<p>A government statement said Prime Minister Meraj Khalid's cabinet had decided to cut the perks of state-owned bank executives, reduce car fleets and guest houses, and disallow club entertainment expenses except for chief executives.</p>
<p>The measures were to &quot;curtail unnecessary and wasteful expenditure being incurred by the nationalised commercial banks and the development finance institutions, which would result in a saving of approximately 2.57 billion rupees ($64 million)&quot;.</p>
</text>
